    <h1>Data processing agreement</h1>
    <p class="meta">Version 1.0, <span class="ph">[go-live date]</span> · <a href="/da/databehandleraftale" hreflang="da">Dansk version</a></p>
    <p class="draft"><b>Draft for legal review.</b> The body is Datatilsynet's standard contractual clauses, unchanged. Only the
      choices and appendices below are Kupro's own text.</p>

    <section class="short" aria-labelledby="short-h">
      <h2 id="short-h">The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You (the customer) are the data controller for everything in your workspace. We are your processor.</li>
        <li>We process it only to run Kupro for you, only in the EU, and only with the sub-processors listed here.</li>
        <li>We give you 30 days' notice before adding a sub-processor, and you can object.</li>
        <li>We tell you about a personal data breach within 48 hours of finding it.</li>
        <li>When you leave, you can export everything; then we delete it.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <h2 id="how">How this agreement works</h2>
    <p>This agreement uses the <b>standard contractual clauses for data processing</b> adopted by the Danish Data Protection Agency
      (Datatilsynet) under GDPR Article 28(8), in the version published by Datatilsynet, as amended in March 2024 (<a href="https://www.datatilsynet.dk/presse-og-nyheder/nyhedsarkiv/2024/mar/aendring-i-datatilsynets-standarddatabehandleraftale">datatilsynet.dk</a>). Those clauses
      (sections 1 to 15) apply word for word between you and Pilgaard Development, CVR 41249269.
      Appendices A to D below complete them.</p>
    <p>If anything in our <a href="/terms">terms of service</a> conflicts with this agreement on the protection of personal data,
      this agreement wins.</p>

    <h2 id="choices">Choices in the clauses</h2>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Clause</th><th>Our choice</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>7.3 Sub-processors</td><td>General written authorisation. We notify you of changes at least <b>30 days</b> ahead.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>10.1 Breach notification</td><td>Without undue delay, and no later than <b>48 hours</b> after we become aware of a breach.</td></tr>
