    <h2 id="a">Appendix A · The processing</h2>
    <h3>A.1 Purpose</h3>
    <p>To provide the Kupro service to the data controller: issue tracking, sprints, the delivery plan, the API, CLI and MCP
      access, GitHub integration, email notifications, and, when the controller uses it, the meeting agent.</p>
    <h3>A.2 Nature of the processing</h3>
    <p>Storage, hosting, backup, search, display and transmission of workspace content; sending emails; transcription of meeting audio
      and generation of suggested issue changes from the transcript.</p>
    <h3>A.3 Types of personal data</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Names, email addresses, roles and capacity (hours per week) of members and guests.</li>
      <li>Any personal data the controller's users put into issues, comments, attachments and descriptions.</li>
      <li>Meeting audio (in memory only, seconds), and transcripts with the words behind each suggestion (until the meeting ends, or as long as the controller sets, at most 365 days).</li>
      <li>Activity history: who changed what, when, and through which surface (web, CLI, MCP, meeting agent).</li>
      <li>Technical data: IP addresses and request logs.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Kupro is not designed for special categories of data (Article 9) or data about criminal convictions. The controller should not put such data in a workspace.</p>
    <h3>A.4 Data subjects</h3>
    <p>The controller's employees, contractors and guests who use Kupro; people mentioned in workspace content; people who speak in a meeting where the meeting agent runs.</p>
    <h3>A.5 Duration</h3>
    <p>As long as the controller has a Kupro workspace, plus the export and deletion periods in C.4.</p>

