    <p>Billing vendors (Alunta, card acquirer) process data we control about the paying company, not workspace content, so they are not sub-processors under this agreement.</p>

    <h2 id="c">Appendix C · Instructions and security</h2>
    <h3>C.1 Instructions</h3>
    <p>The processor processes personal data only to provide Kupro as described in A.1, as the controller configures it in the
      product (for example: which members have access, whether the meeting agent runs, suggest or full auto mode), and as the controller
      instructs in writing.</p>
    <h3>C.2 Security measures</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Encryption</b>: TLS for all traffic. Backups encrypted with AES-256 before they leave the server. Server disks rely on OVHcloud's physical and access security.</li>
      <li><b>Tenant separation</b>: every workspace-owned record carries the workspace id; a database query filter limits every request to the signed-in workspace, and automated tests check it.</li>
      <li><b>Access</b>: production access limited to the founders, with SSH keys and two-factor authentication. Admin consoles behind separate accounts with 2FA.</li>
      <li><b>Authentication</b>: self-hosted Keycloak; hashed passwords; brute-force protection; revocable API and agent tokens.</li>
      <li><b>Meeting audio</b>: held in memory only, never written to disk or logs; transcripts deleted when the meeting ends unless the controller sets a retention period.</li>
      <li><b>Backups</b>: nightly database backups and continuous WAL archiving to EU object storage, kept 35 days; restore tested weekly.</li>
      <li><b>Monitoring</b>: self-hosted logs, traces and metrics kept 30 days; alerts on errors and downtime.</li>
      <li><b>Development</b>: code review, automated tests and dependency updates; secrets kept out of the source code.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>C.3 Assistance to the controller</h3>
    <p>Most data-subject requests can be handled in the product (edit, export, delete). For the rest, we help within 14 days of a
      written request. We also help with impact assessments and prior consultations with information about the processing.</p>
    <h3>C.4 Storage period and deletion</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Meeting audio: seconds, in memory. Transcripts and suggestion snippets: until the meeting ends, or after a day if it is never ended. The controller can set up to 365 days in the workspace settings.</li>
      <li>Workspace content: until the controller deletes it. After the subscription ends, read-only and exportable for 30 days, then deleted.</li>
      <li>Backups: overwritten within 35 days after deletion.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>C.5 Location</h3>
    <p>Processing takes place in the processor's and sub-processors' facilities in the EU listed in appendix B, and by the processor's staff working from the EU.</p>
    <h3>C.6 Transfers to third countries</h3>
    <p>No transfers outside the EU/EEA. Any future transfer requires the controller's prior written instruction and a valid transfer basis under GDPR chapter V.</p>
    <h3>C.7 Audits of the processor</h3>
    <p>Once a year, on request, we send a written statement describing our security measures and any incidents. The controller may
      carry out or commission an on-site or remote audit with 30 days' notice, at its own cost, no more than once a year unless a
      breach or a supervisory authority gives reason.</p>
    <h3>C.8 Audits of sub-processors</h3>
    <p>We review each sub-processor's certifications and data processing terms before use and yearly after that (for example ISO 27001 for OVHcloud and Scaleway).</p>

    <h2 id="d">Appendix D · Other terms</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Liability under this agreement follows section 11 of the <a href="/terms#t11">terms of service</a>, without limiting either party's liability towards data subjects or authorities under GDPR.</li>
      <li>Assistance that goes beyond what the product does on its own and takes more than 2 hours a year may be charged at our usual hourly rate, agreed in advance.</li>
      <li>This agreement ends when the main agreement ends and all personal data is deleted or returned.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="sign">Accepting</h2>
    <p>This agreement is accepted when a workspace owner accepts the terms of service. If you need a signed copy for your records,
      write to <a href="mailto:contact@kupro.app">contact@kupro.app</a> and we send one for e-signature.</p>
